      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>What does NPI cover?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">NPI covers prototype and first-article builds, process qualification and a controlled ramp into volume production.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Is NPI run on the production process?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">NPI uses production-representative lines and processes. The qualified manufacturing process can then carry forward into volume production, reducing the need to establish a new process during ramp.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can an NPI product be qualified at a second Hana site?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. The manufacturing process is documented during qualification, so where a program needs a second source, the product can be qualified at another Hana site in a different country through first-article qualification. Each site is qualified separately against the customer's requirements.</div>
    </details>
